# Entire Activity Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Ship `entire activity`, a tabbed TUI + static-output CLI command that surfaces session/checkpoint/agent activity across selectable time ranges, reusing existing CLI infrastructure and consuming server-authoritative labels from the entire.io api.

**Architecture:** Local-first data model (reads `.git/entire-sessions/` and `entire/checkpoints/v1` tree), with optional async api enrichment for work-mode labels and per-category tool-time. Six tabs (today/range/history/agents/repos/report), each a self-contained panel layout. Activity types are read-only projections over existing `session.State` + `checkpoint.CheckpointSummary` — no new persistence. Visual language inherits the repo's lipgloss palette and extends with semantic label colors, gradient bars, and 5-tier heatmap cells.

**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x · cobra · bubbletea · lipgloss · huh · go-git v6 · existing `cmd/entire/cli/{session,checkpoint,strategy,auth,api,paths,trailers,transcript}` packages.

**Design doc:** `docs/2026-04-15-entire-activity-design.md`

